# Health Investment

Health Investment is the concept of allocating time, money, and effort toward maintaining and improving one's physical and mental well-being as a form of capital allocation. This connects to broader frameworks around [[investment-strategies-for-life-satisfaction]], [[user-investment-habit]], and [[personal-finance]].

The skill card for Health Investment currently has no detailed content, definition, or supporting sources. It is flagged with confidence 0.7 and low priority, last reviewed on 2026-04-18.

Related concepts include investing in habits, risk management of personal health, and the long-term returns on preventive care and wellness practices. Further development of this concept would benefit from connecting to decision-making frameworks such as [[decision-quality-vs-outcome-quality]] and [[expected-value-ev]].